From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: mask first ERL userspace return IRQ

The physical SF2000 reaches the marker immediately after RESTORE_SOME with
Status 0x8815 and EPC 0x004002f0, then watchdog-resets before any syscall,
TLB fault, or generic exception marker. That proves the final saved register
restore completes and leaves the remaining failure in RESTORE_SP_AND_RET.

The restored Status has IE set before RESTORE_SP_AND_RET loads the userspace
stack and executes eret. If this core accepts an interrupt in that window,
Linux would enter the exception path on the userspace stack and die before
the retained exception markers can run. Keep IE clear for the SF2000 ERL
identity-userspace handoff so the first transition cannot be interrupted
between the stack restore and eret. Also move the final-restore marker to the
actual reserved progress header words.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S   | 6 +++---
 arch/mips/kernel/process.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -134,13 +134,13 @@ restore_partial:		# restore partial frame
 	 * No calls here: user registers have been restored and CP0_STATUS may
 	 * already contain the final user/ERL value. k0/k1 are not user ABI
-	 * state, and 0xa13f0010 is the retained progress header reserved area.
+	 * state, and 0xa13f0014 is the retained progress header reserved area.
 	 */
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
 	li	k1, 0x51510001
-	sw	k1, 16(k0)
+	sw	k1, 20(k0)
 	mfc0	k1, CP0_STATUS
-	sw	k1, 20(k0)
+	sw	k1, 24(k0)
 	MFC0	k1, CP0_EPC
-	sw	k1, 24(k0)
+	sw	k1, 28(k0)
 	sync
 #endif
 	RESTORE_SP_AND_RET
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
@@ -114,6 +114,10 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs * regs, unsigned long pc, unsigned long sp)
 	if (sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled()) {
 		status |= ST0_ERL;
 		status &= ~ST0_EXL;
+		/*
+		 * Avoid an interrupt between RESTORE_SP and the final eret.
+		 */
+		status &= ~ST0_IE;
 		sf2000_progress_mark("mips-start-thread-ebase", 9,
 			read_c0_ebase());
 		sf2000_progress_mark("mips-start-thread-errorepc-before", 9,
-- 
2.45.0
